WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.015
Somewhere tonight,

2
00:00:03.015 --> 00:00:07.646
a Marine is finishing work that no one will ever see.

3
00:00:07.896 --> 00:00:09.495
Thirty reconciliations.

4
00:00:09.495 --> 00:00:12.021
A funding gap, caught in time.

5
00:00:12.371 --> 00:00:15.969
By morning, most of it is gone.

6
00:00:16.019 --> 00:00:17.443
Into a spreadsheet.

7
00:00:17.443 --> 00:00:18.186
An inbox.

8
00:00:18.186 --> 00:00:19.736
Somebody’s memory.

9
00:00:21.086 --> 00:00:22.930
Vantage keeps it.

10
00:00:25.386 --> 00:00:27.434
Say what you did, once.

11
00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:32.488
Vantage reads the numbers, and shows you before it saves.

12
00:00:33.038 --> 00:00:36.011
Your section’s work, in one queue.

13
00:00:36.011 --> 00:00:38.508
Claim it, and it’s yours.

14
00:00:38.958 --> 00:00:40.837
Cases follow cited procedures.

15
00:00:40.837 --> 00:00:42.286
Evidence before action.

16
00:00:42.286 --> 00:00:44.308
Resolved only when verified.

17
00:00:44.858 --> 00:00:45.869
Open commitments.

18
00:00:45.869 --> 00:00:47.180
Undelivered orders.

19
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.658
Read in the order the money moves.

20
00:00:51.408 --> 00:00:53.895
Every entry, signed into the history.

21
00:00:53.895 --> 00:00:56.349
Nothing important happens quietly.

22
00:00:56.899 --> 00:01:02.009
And the credit goes to the Marine who did the work.

23
00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:06.883
When evaluation season comes, the record is already written,

24
00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:09.541
and every line cites its source.

25
00:01:10.091 --> 00:01:13.977
Leaders see the whole section at a glance.

26
00:01:14.727 --> 00:01:16.370
Private by default.

27
00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:19.548
Built to run on your own network.

28
00:01:20.498 --> 00:01:21.181
Vantage.

29
00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:24.096
Give good work a lasting record.
